{"duration_api_ms":8955,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8a90ec0e-3b06-4292-9e4d-a3c312bebc55","total_cost_usd":0.0010912,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":733,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1412,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1045},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":733,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1412,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":733},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1276,"outputTokens":1634,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":733,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0010912,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1245,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":733,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Yes, but the benefit is pooled, not reserved for mutual fund holders.\n\n**Mechanism:** Under IRC §852(b)(6), a RIC generally doesn't recognize gain when it distributes appreciated securities in redemption of its shares. When ETF-class holders redeem in kind, the fund hands out low-basis securities, so the embedded gains leave the portfolio without being realized. Because all classes share one portfolio, fewer realized gains means smaller capital gains distributions, which helps every class, including the mutual fund class, in proportion to its NAV.\n\n**Limits:**\n- The benefit depends on ETF-class redemption volume and on which lots are delivered. Gains can still be realized through cash-based trading.\n- Mutual fund redemptions are typically cash, so they can force sales that realize gains, partly offsetting the benefit.\n- Class-level expenses and any costs of in-kind baskets must be allocated among classes under the fund's multi-class plan (Rule 18f-3 framework).\n- Benefits are shared pro rata, so MF holders don't capture a dedicated advantage.","ttft_ms":5962,"type":"result","duration_ms":7732,"uuid":"63703dd5-2320-47f4-b972-0008026bd99c","ttft_stream_ms":473,"time_to_request_ms":94,"first_content_frame_ms":473,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
